CLI.md §3.3, IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md §8.1, API.md W14: `check --watch` prints the whole check first;
after a change, a header, the findings that appeared, then (after the next change) one `fixed:`
line per finding gone, and the summary each time. The interrupt ends it with exit 130.
-- args --
check
--watch
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

const X = 1
-- b/b.canon --
/// B.
package b

const Y = 2
-- step1/a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

const = 1
const X = 1
-- step2/a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

const X = 1
-- want --
[exit 130]
[stdout]
0 errors, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
-- 1 files changed, 1 packages re-checked
error[E1116]  a/a.canon:4:7
  expected IDENT; found =

1 error, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
-- 1 files changed, 1 packages re-checked
fixed: error[E1116]  a/a.canon:4:7

0 errors, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
[stderr]
canon: interrupted
